  "about": "What each NPC host event does in the world (S6; C08: it was a table in the code; schema 2, VILLAGE_PLAN V02). The core's agents raise the events; an event not listed changes nothing. action is give_item (an item by its stable name, and a count: a number, or qty for the number the learner said, capped at 5), point_at_noun (the beacon goes to the nearest block of a catalogue noun), point_at_place (to a named place of the scene) point_at_slot (to the place a slot of the learner's line names, through the scene's labels: villager.point answers \"¿dónde está el río?\" and any other place; a place the scene does not have is answered by <npc>.unknown_place), take_item, sell (a purchase: the learner pays the price for each item asked for, no cap; another item is answered by <npc>.wont_sell, none asked for by <npc>.none_asked, too few coins by <npc>.cant_pay, a full bag by <npc>.no_room) or buy (VILLAGE_PLAN V15, the sale turned round: the NPC pays the price for each item the learner sells; none in the bag is answered by <npc>.cant_sell, another item by <npc>.wont_buy, none offered by <npc>.none_offered, a full bag by <npc>.no_room).",
